# Naming

The class name ends with the role, so a reader can tell what the file does.

- A DTO ends with `Dto`: `CampaignInDto`, `CampaignOutDto`.
- A controller ends with `Controller`: `CampaignController`.
- A service ends with `Service`: `CampaignService`.
- A domain model has no role suffix: `Campaign`, `CampaignDraft`.

The file name matches the class in snake case.

```python
# Bad: the wire body is named like a model
class CampaignOut(BaseModel):
    ...

# Good
class CampaignOutDto(BaseModel):
    """Campaign the client can show."""
```
